okay today I'm going to talk to you  about recycling I'm going to talk to you  about three different aspects of  recycling and why it's so important  because earth's resources won't last  forever  they're finite so it's really important  to be able to recycle so they can last  much longer so the first reason why it's  important to recycle is the idea that it  conserves resources now like I  previously said the amount of material  materials in the world is finite which  means one day that it will run out it's  not unlimited so let's just think about  this let's say we're extracting  aluminium from beneath the earth's  surface every single time we extract  some aluminium from from any Thea  surface we get less and less there's  less and less left so the more and more  that we extract the less and less  missing raw materials we have left  because there's a finite amount that  just means they're limited so instead of  doing this if we if we recycle materials  then those raw materials beneath a  surface or wherever we're going to be  extracting them will last much longer  also if we recycle it requires much less  energy than constantly having to extract  these metals for example the extraction  of aluminium is very expensive because  we have to use electrolysis so there's  one really big reason why it's important  to recycle the second reason is the fact  that it protects the environment and  environment so as we can see let's think  about this this idea here when we  extract metals from the ground we need  to we need to mind for them so when  we're mining for them it can it can  basically destroy habitats so animals  might have been living in this area and  then we built this mine and the habitats  have been destroyed so that's one reason  why recycling instead of building loads  of mine  and extracting it from the ground is a  positive thing also we need to consider  landfill sites so a landfill site is  quite simply where we go and dump loads  and loads of our rubbish that we throw  away rather than recycling so you know  trucks Laureus might take all of this  all of this waste here and just dump it  in these huge piles it's called a  landfill  now landfill is bad for the environment  because first of all it takes up loads  of space and secondly it can really  pollute the environment which is put  into so there protect the environment is  another reason why you can recycle  because if we're recycling for reusing  and reforming products we don't have to  dump it into these huge landfill sites  now the final one I'm going to talk  about the final advantage of recycling  to talk about is economic benefits so  economics is to do with money so it's  actually a good way to be able to to  generate money or save money because if  we recycle we're doing a couple of  things first of all we can have lots of  people employed there's jobs made  available secondly we don't have to  spend loads and loads of money on  extracting our raw materials for example  less less money if I was extracting  aluminium would have to be spent on  electrolysis if we can just reuse it  we're saving lots and lots of money also  we can create new products we can create  recycled products and if we if we sell  those products again we can make money  from them rather than just chuck it into  a landfill site where we can know well  they're no longer be used if they could  be turned into something new we can then  sell those new things and we can  generate more money so just to summarize  there's three big reasons why it's  important to recycle first  for conserving resources which are  finite which means one day they'll run  out protecting the environment from  building mines and landfill and finally  economic benefits by creating jobs  saving money on extracting raw materials  and being able to sell those recycled  products thank you very much
 

